# The six strict-f64 builtin contracts — `abs`, `min`, `max`, `sqrt`,
# `atan2`, `sign` — as one runnable pinned witness.
#
# The strict-f64 registry emitter admits these calls end-to-end since
# emath-s9w1m + fpl60 (previously they diagnosed `unknown function in
# strict-f64 subset`); this file is the probe artifact for that
# admission.  Contracts of record:
#   abs(x)       piecewise: `x < 0 -> -x`, else `x`.
#   min/max(a,b) piecewise selection of the smaller/larger operand.
#   sqrt(x)      domain obligation `SqrtNonNegative` on the CALLER: a
#                negative operand yields the IEEE NaN VALUE on the
#                Float64 carrier (per the IEEE-754 contract in
#                reference/types-units-shapes-and-domains.md), it does
#                not refuse at parse; discharge the obligation as an
#                assumption or a checked constraint before the call.
#   atan2(y, x)  the IEEE two-argument arctangent, correctly rounded.
#   sign(x)      mathematical sgn: `-1 / 0 / +1`, exactly `0` at zero.
# Exact-first: every pin below is exactly representable or a single
# correctly-rounded IEEE constant, verified independently.
#
# Runnable (no Cargo; generic EMIR + reference-VM lane):
#   emath eval language/examples/intro/clamp-distance-builtins.emath --set x=-3 --set y=7 --set v=9 --set b=3.7
# `emath test` on this file builds and runs the one pinned example
# block (Phase 1: one evaluate target per test-bearing declaration, so
# all six builtin probes ride in the single packed vector).
#
# The clamp is composed from the audited builtins:
# `min(max(v, min(x, y)), max(x, y))` clamps `v` into the window
# [min(x, y), max(x, y)] — the abs/min/max-in-a-clamp context.

emath function builtin_six_contracts:
    inputs:
        x: Float64
        y: Float64
        v: Float64
        b: Float64
    outputs:
        packed: Vector[Float64]
    definitions:
        abs_pin = abs(x)
        min_pin = min(x, y)
        max_pin = max(x, y)
        clamp_pin = min(max(v, min(x, y)), max(x, y))
        packed = [abs_pin, min_pin, max_pin, clamp_pin,
                  sqrt(4.0), sqrt(2.25), sqrt(0.0),
                  atan2(1.0, 1.0), atan2(1.0, 0.0),
                  sign(b), sign(0.0), sign(-2.5)]
    goals:
        evaluate <packed>:
            produce rust.library
    tests:
        example <six_contracts_pinned>:
            given x = -3.0
            given y = 7.0
            given v = 9.0
            given b = 3.7
            expect packed == [3.0, -3.0, 7.0, 7.0, 2.0, 1.5, 0.0, 0.7853981633974483, 1.5707963267948966, 1.0, 0.0, -1.0]

    compile:
        target rust
        profile library
        numeric strict-f64
